 票券: https://appointments.library.stanford.edu/event/18003817\n\nWith t
 he launch of the United Nations System Data Commons last month\, semantic 
 search has arrived to international government data. How is semantic searc
 h enabled for data\, and which organizations use it?\n\nWe will explore ge
 nerative artificial intelligence's role in international government data\,
  with a focus on the SDMX metadata standard\, OECD's "AI for data\, data f
 or AI" initiative\, an IMF paper entitled "StatGPT"\, and practical advice
  on using AI with this valuable data source.\n\nFeel free to bring questio
 ns about finding\, accessing\, and using data from sources like the UN\, E
 uropean Union\, World Bank\, IMF\, OECD\, International Labour Organizatio
 n\, and International Organization for Migration.
